1	//! Intl.Locale and likely subtags.
2	//!
3	//! Slots (own data properties, in this order): `__locale_tag` (canonical
4	//! tag), `__locale_basename`, `__locale_language`, `__locale_script`,
5	//! `__locale_region`, `__locale_variants` (joined with "-") when present,
6	//! then one `__locale_<key>` per -u- keyword (sorted by key; "" for a
7	//! keyword without value).  Getters and methods require an object
8	//! (`TypeError: not a Locale`) with an own string `__locale_tag`
9	//! (`TypeError: receiver is not an Intl.Locale`); `baseName` / `language`
10	//! additionally need their string slots.
11	//!
12	//! The constructor canonicalises the tag, applies the options (language,
13	//! script, region, variants, calendar, collation, firstDayOfWeek, hourCycle,
14	//! caseFirst, numeric, numberingSystem -- read and validated in this order)
15	//! and canonicalises again (so `drw` -> `prs` -> `fa-AF`).
16	//!
17	//! `maximize` / `minimize` use the original's likely-subtags data
18	//! (`locale_data.rs`, CLDR-based, extracted from the original).  The
19	//! `get*` info methods are trivial in the original: the -u- value or
20	//! `gregory` / `default` / `h23` / `latn`, time zones `["UTC"]` when a region
21	//! is present, text direction always `ltr`, week info
22	//! `{firstDay: fw (mon=1..sun=7, default 1), weekend: [6, 7]}`.
23	
